  "body": "## What changed\n- New verification-gate clause `posting::wcs_rotation::rotated_wcs_problems` (`crates/app/src/posting_wcs_rotation.rs`), called from `verification_report`, so the one-file post, the per-op post and the script API all refuse. It produces one line per rotated offset entity a posted op uses:\n  `setup Setup1: its work offset G54 is rotated 90.000 deg about Z; posting a rotated work offset is not supported yet - re-align it without rotation or post from an unrotated setup (operations: Face1)` (in a legacy document with no setups it reads `work offset G54 is rotated ...`).\n- The op-to-slot law moved into `wcs_rotation::wcs_slot`. `wcs_context` and the clause both read it, so the gate judges exactly the offset that gets posted.\n- Tolerance: an angle (`2*atan2(|xyz|,|w|)`) of at most 1e-9 rad counts as unrotated, so identity offsets post byte-identical.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/315-rotated-wcs.md`. G68/G68.2, CYCLE800/ROT, PLANE/CYCL 10 and baking the rotation into coordinates were all set aside for now because none is trivially verifiable. That is step 3 of #315.\n\n## Readings\n- Reproduced first. With the clause disabled, a G54 turned 90 deg about Z posts without error (`a_rotated_work_offset_is_refused_by_name`, `a_setups_rotated_offset_names_the_setup` and `an_unrotated_offset_posts_exactly_as_before` fail at the `expect_err`). The record stream is identical to the stream for the square offset (`the_post_stream_carries_no_offset_rotation`).\n- Quick gate, debug, all green: posting 17, conformance 6, fanuc_post 8, golden_cl 23, per_op_files 9, post_not_judged 4, setups 11, wcs_align 5, probe_op 11, tormach_post 10, lathe_post 7, scripting 17, machine 32, drilling_cross_stock 8, rotary_verify 9, rotated_wcs 4. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean. No golden changed.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`crates/app/tests/rotated_wcs.rs`: `the_post_stream_carries_no_offset_rotation`, `a_rotated_work_offset_is_refused_by_name`, `a_setups_rotated_offset_names_the_setup`, `an_unrotated_offset_posts_exactly_as_before`.\n\nChangelog: A work offset with a rotation (3-2-1 alignment) is now refused at post by name instead of posting coordinates in the unrotated frame\n\nFixes #315\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
